WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.483
Learn to compare graphs in which the same data has been displayed and explain how

00:00:05.483 --> 00:00:10.414
they are the same and different and find examples of graphs in which many-to-one

00:00:10.414 --> 00:00:14.641
correspondence is used in print and electronic media, such as newspapers, magazines

00:00:14.641 --> 00:00:17.459
and the internet, and describe the correspondence used

00:00:18.283 --> 00:00:24.021
A table lists orange: 26 and banana: 8. How many more are in the larger group? The

00:00:24.021 --> 00:00:27.734
answer is 18. Subtract the smaller bar height from the larger.

00:00:28.617 --> 00:00:33.923
A bar chart shows mangoes: 24 and bananas: 11. What is the difference between their

00:00:33.923 --> 00:00:37.107
bars? Pause and solve it in your exercise book.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:41.065
The answer is 13. Subtract the smaller count.
